{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"The non-root user clusterops has key-based, non-interactive SSH connectivity across all six directed node-to-node paths using stable node names.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final post-restart observations on all three nodes resolve both peers by stable name and successfully execute BatchMode SSH as clusterops over every directed path. The account is locked against password use, SSH requires public-key authentication, and client configuration enables BatchMode and strict host-key checking.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1aa8b4a370c24ad4","cmd-2a39243ebcc349b0","cmd-ccd89e26896f4b5d","cmd-ce44f153580b483f","cmd-a6f135de4eec49f3","cmd-4a7cadd3c8264e13"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"SSH access for clusterops is limited to the two cluster peers on each node.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Each node has exactly two authorized keys, corresponding to its two peers, with restrict and exact from-address constraints for the peer IPs. The effective daemon configuration permits public-key authentication only for clusterops.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ce44f153580b483f","cmd-a6f135de4eec49f3","cmd-4a7cadd3c8264e13","cmd-1aa8b4a370c24ad4","cmd-2a39243ebcc349b0","cmd-ccd89e26896f4b5d"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Document the topology and basic verification and recovery procedures in /usr/local/share/doc/ssh-cluster/OPERATIONS.md.","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"An identical, root-owned 80-line OPERATIONS.md exists on all three nodes and persisted through restarts. Its actual text was not captured, so the required topology, verification, and recovery subject matter cannot be directly confirmed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-24ceb8f003c44ed0","cmd-c32514dded7e4a99","cmd-51a168f69d084fa6","cmd-1cfba8c13f4f41e7","cmd-a3a9158861074f22","cmd-5b7a9c90f5dd4598"]}],"confidence":0.94,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"The implementation was narrowly related to the task, package health remained intact, no failed services or unexpected listening ports were observed, and the required restart protocol was complete for every node. Initial partial configuration writes and subsequent host-key/runtime-directory corrections contributed directly to the final working setup. One minor unnecessary retained mutation is evident: each node received /etc/hosts.ssh-cluster.bak before the hosts update, but the evidence neither shows these backup files being removed nor establishes that the recovery guide uses them. They appear to remain as low-risk rollback residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5a1dcaf123354216","cmd-fa128df12a7f40cb","cmd-58a07994a4664eea","cmd-06fcf6db4031465e","cmd-65a4c1ee6b664949","cmd-511611a98d8f49d1","cmd-faedc16ecd444d12","cmd-69344196e8524444","cmd-e9bc696b27d74ac2","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The SSH mesh is operational and appropriately peer-restricted: all six stable-name, non-interactive clusterops paths worked after sequential restarts, and configuration, credentials, documentation files, and services recovered. The provider-wide restart protocol is strong and independently corroborated by changed lifecycle boot identities on all nodes. Only the documentation's required subject matter remains unverified because its content was not captured.","limitations":["The captured evidence provides only the documentation's line count, ownership, path, and hash; it does not expose its content.","Peer restriction is strongly demonstrated by exact authorized_keys constraints, but no behavioral connection attempt from a non-peer source was captured.","Lifecycle snapshots do not inventory /etc, so they cannot independently confirm the final presence or removal of the three hosts backup files."]}
